{# Decision template: does the target accept the speaker's offer to stop fighting? One yes/no question.
   Sent by Injury_Engine.dll (TruceDecision.cpp) through PublicSendCustomDecisionToLLM when an NPC uses the
   Stop_Fighting action on another NPC (the player as target is never asked). Rendered into a decisions request,
   never into chat messages. Yes: both stand down and stay calm for a day. No: the speaker stands down, the target
   may fight on.

   Context pushed by the game (C++ snapshot): speaker_uuid, speaker_name, target_uuid, target_name, relationship
   (Skyrim relationship rank: lovers .. archnemeses, or strangers), speaker_health / target_health (unhurt |
   lightly hurt | badly hurt | near death), speaker_is_follower, target_is_follower, target_fights_speaker,
   timeline [lines, oldest first: the target's recent speech, narrations and events; hits, combat and spells left out]. #}
[ state target ]
{{ target_name }}{% if target_is_follower %}, a follower of the player{% endif %}, is {{ target_health }}{% if target_fights_speaker %} and is fighting {{ speaker_name }}{% endif %}.
{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", target_uuid) }}
[ end state ]

[ state speaker ]
{{ speaker_name }}{% if speaker_is_follower %}, a follower of the player{% endif %}, is {{ speaker_health }} and offers to stop fighting.
{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", speaker_uuid) }}
[ end state ]

[ state fight ]
{{ target_name }} and {{ speaker_name }} are {{ relationship }}.
{{ target_name }} is {{ target_health }}; {{ speaker_name }} is {{ speaker_health }}.
[ end state ]

[ state timeline ]
{% if length(timeline) > 0 %}
{% for line in timeline %}
{{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
Nothing notable has happened recently.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question accept noul ]
Does {{ target_name }} accept {{ speaker_name }}'s offer to stop fighting right now?
Leans yes: {{ target_name }} is losing or badly hurt, the two are friends, allies or lovers, both are followers of the player, or the fight looks like a misunderstanding (`timeline`).
Leans no: they are enemies or sworn foes, {{ target_name }} is winning while {{ speaker_name }} is badly hurt, or `timeline` shows a grudge, an insult or a reason to keep fighting.
[ end question ]
